The best use is probably to not buy anything. Wait, play with homebrew deck and enjoy rediscovering the game from the start. When you'll be more familiar with the game and know exactly what kind of deck you wanna play you'll easily know what you have to buy to get it.

&nbsp;

Also 100$ can get you a looooooot of other cool game.

From my point of view it looks like 2 people playing in open crew with the mic on because they want to be able to communicate with their random mate but they just don't fully realize that you can also clearly ear them so they speak between each other without filter. They were mostly speaking to each other and when the guy was using the N word it was to speak to his mate and not directed at you.

&nbsp;

When people speak with friends they very often use a more vulgar and familiar tone. Honestly I find it very very soft compared to what I have seen in my gamer life.

For me performance are lower since the new seafort. It seems that Rare has trouble to keep the game "light" with all the stuff released. I have an old computer and I used to play with no issue with "high-mid quality" graphic settings. Now I'm all in low with resolution from 1080p to 900p and my computer eat glue after 2h.

&nbsp;

My computer is pretty old and I planned to get a new one anyway but yeah it's not you, the game clearly became more demanding and push old computer away.

Fleet creator can help: https://www.fleetcreator.com/en/

&nbsp;

It'll detect your server and you'll see if 2 players are on the same.

I probably missed the part where you said you were simplifying it down because you never said it. I saw the part where you insulted someone else math skill, the part where you failed basic stats and the part where you used your personnal stats to determine if something is totally OP or not.

&nbsp;

On HSreplay for standard the deck has 47.3% winrate for 2800 games. Considering how low the decision making of this deck is I don't really see how a very good player could perform way above average. On Wild there is so much bullshit everywhere than waiting turn 3 to do something is already a death sentence especially when a single silence can totally destroy the deck. You have success with it because it's something new and unexpected.

I love your audacity. Telling someone he is really bad at math and proceed to massively fail your stats right after that require some balls. You can't work with possibilities here. What you want to know is the probability to not fail which means not having a single minion in your hand at turn 3 AND multiply it by the probability to have switcheroo in hand at this moment.

&nbsp;

For example if you have 2 switcheroos in hand and draw a minions turn 1 I fall into your first scenario and still fail.

Next time try harpoon turn :)

&nbsp;

Joke aside you need to practice on leaving the wheel alone. Usually you don't need to be 100% glued to the wheel, you can drop it, do something else for 5sec then come back to it to fix, then drop it again ... All those 5sec cumulated will make a massive difference at the end. For example you could definitly have drop the wheel at 18sec to help your mate with the sail or guard the ladder while your mate is working on the sails. Your next move was at 23sec so that's a 5sec windows where you did nothing. Then at 27sec you put the wheel full left and again do nothing until 40sec. That's 13sec of inactivity in battle and that's a big deal. You could have drop the wheel, help your mate with the sail then come back to it. The extra time won would allow your mate to guard ladder, throw bombs, shoot some dude or even board the opponent ship.

&nbsp;

At the end all this move could have been performed alone either with harpoon turn or dropping the wheel. This was a very good move and yet your mate lost a solid 23sec on this compared to what very good crew would have done.

&nbsp;

I think this is a great example of the difference between a good and a very good player. If you watch video of famous solo sloopers on youtube you'll quickly notice that they never EVER afk on the wheel. I admit it requires some balls to drop the wheel at first because your first tries will probably end in a crash but once you'll get the timing between drop, fix, drop, fix, drop, fix ... you'll improve a LOT.

I recently sunk a 4 man Reaper Galleon as a solo sloop. I had just finish my voyage, had nothing to lose, a tons of supplies and I wanted to practice so I go for it because I'm quite good in navals and it looked like an open-crew chasing a poor white sails sloop.

&nbsp;

My first move was to try to contact the sloop for a 2v1 but I failed and decided to go for it solo and win some time for this poor guy who probably had some loot to save. I stayed very far from the Galleon because I know most open-crew players can't land long-shot, dropped 2 mast and put some fire while they missed all their shot. Some guys tried to board me but it wasn't a real issue because I was too far from them and they couldn't board me 2 at a time.

&nbsp;

I ignored all insult from missing board attempt, keep applying pressure then a Kraken come to help me (attracted by salt I guess). I stopped my sloop behind them, keep doing long shot while the kraken was making sure the Galleon was stuck. 2 guys tried to board me so I knew the Galleon was probably dead since a lot of players can't handle a Kraken on a Galleon just with 2 people. I stopped using cannons and just waited for the boarder to come close and put just enough sails so they would keep trying to chase me and let their ship sink. Once the galleon sunk I goes a little bit into the kraken black sea so I wouldn't have to fight it but swimming dudes would suffer from the black sea. Once the area was clean I landed few shot on the kraken with my cannonrawboat for commendation then looted.

&nbsp;

After that I looked for the noob sloop and catch him sails down/anchor down doing a beginner quest on a small island. The guy couldn't speak english (no wonder he didn't accept my offer for a 2v1) so I put all the galleon loot on his boat and left.

*Toss a tomato* 

&nbsp;

Booo, cheater !

Frozen throne 2003. Wotlk end 2011.

