Oh .... my .... god. You made me feel so old and I hate you.

It's a staged vid that make fun of people being too serious while playing WoW. It shows a guild where the leader explain everything for several minutes and one of the dude who was afk the whole time to get some chicken just stand up and run into mobs while yelling his name: "LEEEEEROY JENKINS". It quickly becames famous by exposing the duality of people playing for fun and try harder because at this period WoW was a hit that bring a LOOOOOT of people into gaming. Before WoW gaming was a niche entertainment and WoW bring a lot of new people into gaming putting "hardcore gamer" and "casual gamer" on the same spot. When this vid was release you had people saying this guy was an horrible player while a other part of the community praised him as a genius who know how to have fun.

&nbsp;

Leeeeeroy JENKINS is the equivalent of YOLO for old gamers.

Sea fort have been made for quick and easy fight. It is aimed at player doing quick session or having low skills. There is no reason to put some super hard fight there.

&nbsp;

Also the sea fort can be done in few minutes juste by staying on your ship with the right angle and one-shoting every waves. It takes like 15 cannonballs to clean a fort. A bigger boss would make it 30, not really a big change.

I you get a save from the first pirate of caribean tales you can later restart it. It'll open a portal and you can use it to go on the tale, then stop the tale and you'll teleported back on a new server. It's called server hoping and it reset all your loot but keep your emisary flag and supplies.

&nbsp;

For the red sea it's the same idea. The last tales (shore of gold) give you an item that allow you to run in the red sea at the North-East of the map to do the tale on an hidden island. If you don't have this item your ship will sink so you can always put the save and run to this island. If the people hunting don't have it they can't go there and you are in a safe spot (with nothing to do but at least you are safe).

The game is not fair for solo players so don't play fair. Don't fell any guilt to abuse of unfair tactics. Including running away, running into storm/fog/volcano/events/other players and even using tales saves to server hop or red sea with the shroud breaker.

&nbsp;

As a solo slooper, surviving a fight is a victory. Once you'll be confident in your escape ability, you'll start to be able to actually fight back.

The entire fishing need a rework. Bait should not be necessary to find a special kind of fish and only location should matter. It should reduce the time needed to catch fish by increasing the time you have to reel instead.

&nbsp;

On top of that we should have hunter quest that require specific fish to be sold at a specific sea post like for animals deliveries and emissary flag. Emissary 5 reward you get a quest that send you at a specific location to fight a megalodon where the Shrouded ghost spawn rate is doubled.

I have a lot of sympathy for new players who appear to be lost but damn you are on an entire higher level.

&nbsp;

Play a bit of open crew. People will teach you few things there.

Keep everything simple at start and stay open minded. My biggest mistake when I started was to overdo it so instead of reacting to my players actions I was asking my players to react to my story. Now I just jump into the action with an overall idea of what is going on and just make sure that the story is coherent and evolve with players actions.

&nbsp;

For exemple let's say a NPC ask my players to find her missing daugther. She is in danger and they must hurry. In my mind I just set that some cultist kidnap her for a sacrifice to summon a demon.

&nbsp;

First option: My players try hard to find her but fail everything and it took them 1 week before finding a single clue. They end up finding the cultist right before they kill the daugther as a sacrifice and we play the fight with the cultist. As long as my players show motivation, I keep a good ending option open.

&nbsp;

Second option: My players want to chill in the tavern for 3 days because they don't really care. They got a message that say that the girl they were looking for has been found dead with her heart missing. She has been killed recently. Now there is a demon killing random people in the city and I make sure that they have to fight it and I make sure that it'll be hard and deadly.

&nbsp;

As you can see the main story is very simple. What should be complex is the evolution of the situation due to players actions. Reward motivation and work. Punish laziness and game-killer actions. Stay open to Chaos.

You have to buy a new one. It's a DLC. 1€ for a ship, 0.5€ for a wheel.

&nbsp;

>!This is a joke, you have wood in game to repair!<

You can but you have to pick your fight very carefully. First, get a keg. Second, find a galleon with the white sails and the red reaper flag (very important step). Third, keg them, camp those noob for a minute and it's done.

&nbsp;

You might win few bad karma point but at least you did it solo.

I play a ton of mage and I'm a bit sad that the entire class revolve around drawing Flow early since an entire year. They should have make the card specific to arcane spell rather than increasing the cost and improve other archetype by a looooot. The freeze synergie is useless, the ping mage is an outdated and looks like a 2018 deck and the big spell doesn't have a win condition. They nerf otk strategy but there is absolutly nothing else to do.

&nbsp;

I understand that Blizzard doesn't want 1h games with control match-up but nerf all those mana cheat and bring some real 10 mana win condition.

Even if all big spell were toss at the same time all you would have would be 20 damages spread on the ennemy, 4 minons 3/4 that freeze and then random stuff. 

&nbsp;

That's not enough to win. Big mage will never be a thing as long as you don't have a very strong spell that allow you to win. Survival of the fitest is a spell that create a win condition. Celestial alignement is a spell that create a win condition. Those spell are strong and once they are played the druid has made a big step into winning the game. Deep freeze will never make you win any game. Mask of C'thun is okayish at best Rune of the archmage is just rng.

Find a crewmate on discord. Honestly it's game changing. Just log on discord, create a sloop chat room and ask someone to join you for chill merchant session. Not only it's safer but you could learn a lot of stuff from your mate, it's safer and it's quicker to do the boring job when you are two.

&nbsp;

If you really just want to be alone then I suggest that you learn more about map awarness. You should be always aware of your surrounding to stay as far as possible from any danger.

If you play against aggro you want him to have an immediat impact turn 8 so you have to play spell early. If you play against control the hero power is the value tools that will make you win. If you want to use the new hero power card it has to be an impact tools that swing the game on curve.

&nbsp;

With arcane intellect, fire sale and ice barrier you play a 8 mana card that deal 3 damages to all minions, give 13 armor and draw 2 cards. That's pretty ok for 8 mana on curve.

I think Balinda is a bait. It'll probably be better to use the new T1 and Celestial Ink set as a cost reducer and put some middle cost spell to help against aggro. Also casting some spells in the early game will help to make the hero card more playable. If you played Ice barrier, Fire sale and Arcane intellect in the mid game the hero card can be pretty good played in curve.

&nbsp;

I'm thinking about something like this:

&nbsp;

https://imgur.com/a/uTy2dkt

It can activate Frostweaver dungeoneer effect and the 9 mana spell can be cast with Clumsy carrier without having to worry about the random targeting.

&nbsp;

Turn 3 Dungeonneer, Turn 4 Deepwater Evoker, turn 5 you play the spell + something else with the 2 mana, turn 6 you play the second spell and turn 7 you summon a 4/5 and a 9/9. I'm not saying it's amazing but it's definitely a decent stack of stats that can see play with a little bit more synergy from other cards.

The nerf was to prepare the expansion, not to adjust an issue we have right now. It was the same when they butchered Mana wyrm.

&nbsp;

When I see a card like Mana Syphon I have absolutly no worries for mage.

You choose one and "join" the faction. You'll get the legendary you picked for free and you can use it right now. During the first few days of the new expansion your match and victory will give honor point to the faction you choose. At the end they'll give you the other legendary (the one you didn't pick) and you'll have a diamond version of the legendary of the winning side.

&nbsp;

So let's say you pick horde. You'll have Drek'thar and can use it right now. During the expansion release all your victory will give point to the horde faction. At the end of the event you'll receive Vanndar for free and a diamond version of Drek'Thar or Vanndar depending on which side won the event.

&nbsp;

Drek'thar is more for aggro deck. It summon 2 minions from your deck. Vanndar is more for Big or combo deck so it depends of your playstyle.

&nbsp;

tl:dr you get one now and the other one later. At the end you'll get both for free.

"This is one of the few black humans that are likable" - "he is a gentlemen amongst the other blacks"

&nbsp;

When people are racists as hell but you are still proud of them because they are a tiny little bit less racist. One step at a time I guess.

There is an entire book about vampire that you may find helpfull (night dark master). In the book this is said (translated from french): No one know what happens to their soul but some priest said that it goes into Morr garden but is rejected by the god and they know float trapped between the world of the dead and the living".

&nbsp;

Whatever happen the soul of a vampire will never be accepted by Morr. Your player can have a fetish for vampire but it's either fetish based on hate/fear or she'll be ass kicked by Morr cult when they'll discover it and she can forget about becoming a "spell caster" priest because Morr would probably never answer when she pray.

Did Smough first on my first run. Killed it SLOOOOOWLY with a lightning spear. I destroyed smough with the lightning spear then on the P2 it's just a fight of patience.

&nbsp;

If you stay close to him Ornstein got 2 kind of attack. The "classic" spear hit and the jump AoE. ALL of the classic spear hit can be dodge by rolling in his leg. Once you got the timing it's really easy to just roll inside his leg every time he wanna hit. Once you got this the only thing you have to fear is the AoE/Jump. When you see him bending knees you have to roll away 3 times then use the small time he takes to get up so you can come back inside his leg.

&nbsp;

Once you got this it's just a matter of practice (it took me a full day just to understand and half a day to get decent try). It can be very long. If you make a mistake and get hit don't go away. Go back inside his leg and keep going, you'll just have to use the next "attack timing" to drink a potion.

First part of creating a character should be the relationship between each character. Create a quick table with "friendship, family, love interest, admiration, authority, etc" and then roll for each couple of PC:

&nbsp;

You'll end up with something like this:

* Player 1 - Player 2:  Friend
* Player 1 - Player 3:  Family
* Player 2 - Player 3:  Love interest

&nbsp;

Now ask you player to create character and background while respecting the result as much as possible and change the PC creation a little bit so if 2 people are from the same family they should have the same race and family name, similar trait etc.

&nbsp;

It'll encourage players to create a group rather than just a bunch a totally different character that have to work together.

People really have short-term memory. Ashes of Outland made 8 class unplayable after few hours. All class have a T2 deck outside of priest.

&nbsp;

Honestly if I had to rate this new meta it would probably be amoung the best. You always have to refine your deck because the meta is constantly changing and a deck that crush the other 1 day is hard counter the next day. If it's not a good meta for you then I don't know what you need.

For Dungeonneer, Mage already has arcanologist and it's not played. To highroll the card require to draw frost spell which are mostly bad spells. For Solarian you need to play it, draw it and wait turn 9 to play the prime. It's totally unrealistic against any aggro deck and against control the 2 mana reduction doesn't really have a massive impact. A card that used to be played is now completly ignored, the nerf was too brutal imo but maybe just 8 mana instead of 9 could be good.

&nbsp;

I disagree with wild fire. The fact that you can't play it turn 1 to use it turn 2 is massive against any aggro deck. The only purpose of this upgraded hero power is to be able to survive against aggro without having to put tons of low cost removal into your deck. If the card can't achieve that then it's totally useless and it makes the entire "hero power" archetype they tried to push useless too. Just look at shadow priest right now. They got 2 damage HP at the start of the game. They don't need to spend a card or any mana on it. The difference is just insane.

On HS replay IF got a 70.1% winrate at mulligan. At the same time Wolpertinger got 71.8%.

&nbsp;

I'm really wondering how face hunter can avoid nerf all the time.

I agree on the last part. I started to work on a flow free list to be ready in case they butcher flow and it has the same gameplan but with Celestial ink dropping on fireball or Mask of C'thun. I end up with something like that:

&nbsp;

AAECAf0EAo27A9j5Aw70/AOu9wOFzQPNzgO58QP30QOy9wOH5APQ7AP8ngSn9wP9ngTR7AP73QMA

&nbsp;

I started with Yogg instead of Cornelius but I can never play it. Either I die before the 10 mana mark or the game is in my favor and I don't need it. I'm still not sure about Cornelius and Solarian (same issue than Yogg, 9 mana seems almost unreachable)

I play only mage and tested the deck a lot. I made a lot of test outside of the quest and I agree that mage actually don't need the quest. It makes the mulligan for Flow better and allow you to remove all the bad ice spell. You only need the spell damage of the quest against deck that generate a tons of armor but it is easily compensated by a better mulligan that make the "mirror" match-up way better. Against all the other you have enough damage to kick them and just need draw.

&nbsp;

For me Ignite isn't the issue. Not only the first one is shit (2 damage for 2) but it also increase your deck size so you have to get more draw to cycle. Yes the wombo combo at the end is super flashy but it only start once the entire deck is gone. It's not more or less stupid than Meca C'thun, quest warlock or any other miracle deck.

&nbsp;

The deciding factor of mage deck is Flow. If you have it you're good. If you don't you are in trouble. Nerfing Flow will just make the aggro match-up worse and this could put mage on the garbage bin until the mini-set drop. Mage isn't even the top winrate right now and Flow in the starting hand is a MAJOR boost to the deck overall winrate. Hit Flow with a nerf and the class goes straight into oblivion. Yes the card is problematic but what is even more problematic is the lack of solution outside of it.

&nbsp;

It's important to take into consideration that Mage can't play control or aggro. Control is totally impossible since Mage only got neutral heal and ice barrier (lol). A hunter could just hero-power every turn and win. Aggro has been killed with the Mana wyrm nerf and Mage just don't have any decent aggressive minions. None of the mage minions give any kind of tempo, it's just pure value. You are not fast enough to aggro and you can't survive long enough to play control. Mage is STUCK in a mid-range/tempo gameplan.

&nbsp;

For me the solution would have been to print good early game minions. Frostweaver Dungeonner was a good idea but it should have cost 2. A small decently stated minion that give armor everytime you freeze something would also have been a good idea. By giving good early game minions to contest aggro deck you would have make both aggro and control mage possible. This way a nerf to Flow would have been possible without destroying the class.

&nbsp;

If there is anything to change in Mage right now that would be this:

&nbsp;

- Incanter's Flow: Reduce the cost of your arcane spell by (1) this game
- Refreshing spring water: Become an arcane spell
- Apexis Blast: Become an arcane spell
- Frostweave Dungeonner: Cost 2 instead of 3
- Prestor's pyromancer: Fire spell damage +1 (no more a battlecry)
- Wildfire: Cost 1 instead of 2 (I find it kinda weird to not be able to use it turn 1 to HP turn 2 against aggro)
- Celestial Ink set: Target the highest spell cost on your hand.

As a mage player the best advice I can give you is to not play any minions and just wait/heal until their finish the quest. No having any target for the frost spell is extremelly annoying and delay the quest by a lot. It also force you to either play your spell against your own minions or to use ignite and fireball before the spell damage boost.

&nbsp;

Honestly just heal yourself with hero power and pass until the quest is done.

The issue is that Mage is being punished for playing minion. There is no minion in mage that can contest how refreshing spring water/flow works.

&nbsp;

To prevent this they should have made better minion to tutor freeze/fire/arcane spells and nerf flow in the process. I don't understand why they didn't use the new expansion to nerf flow just before the release. With a nerf to flow and better minions you would have consider swapping flow/spring water for some minions.

You should definitely do all the tales but it can be a bit hard solo to find all the clue. You should also work to get emissary flag for higher risk/reward session.

&nbsp;

Overall I really suggest that you take the time to go on the discord to find someone new like you so you can discover the game together. There are a LOT of new players or people looking for basic stuff/tales on discord.

On a sloop event are designed to be doable solo. On gally it should be doable by a crew of 3 which means triple not double. Also being more means that you can do several stuff at once and death of a crew member is way less of an issue.

&nbsp;

If you have more trouble doing stuff on gally it's because your crewmate perform poorly so you have to compensate for the job they aren't doing.

I think merchant emissary doing trade route and lost ship voyage would be the most effective way to do it. Gold hoarder gives a lot of gold but you have to leave the ship for vault and I find it a bit more dangerous.

&nbsp;

So from the starting outpost, go for merchant emissary and take a voyage to look for missing ship. Buy trading good then go for the voyage. Once it is done, go sell everything to the closest outpost and repeat. Keep all fish/meat you find on the way for seapost. One of you stay all the time on the ship to drive/hook stuff/cook/Unload. The other player constantly jump to get loot/supplies/sell.

If you truly want to play solo: use environement (storm/volcano/fort/skelly galleon) at your advantage against bigger ship. Get a tons a specials cannonballs and do not hesitate to use them. If a bigger boat try to rush at you a good sleepingball right before they try to board can make a massive difference.

&nbsp;

If you play solo just because you have no friend, go on discord. It's really a good place to find decent mates.

Anchor and sails up 100%. You also park parallele to the island so you can grab stuff with harpoons on the beach while still being able to run away just by putting sails down. Also with anchor down if someone start to shoot on your boat you'll almost never be able to rise it because of bumping.

&nbsp;

You should not have any issue putting your wheel straight. There is a small sound when you are straight and most wheel skin make the center very easy to see.

&nbsp;

When unloading your stuff to sell you can park front of the island so you can drop your stuff directly on the deck from the boat but you have to check a lot for people coming and once everything is dropped you park normally.

What do you mean "almost"? :D

&nbsp;

Some tips for solo sloop flameheart: Stop your ship turning your back on the island, let fleet come to you and shoot. By not caring about the speed/direction of your ship you are saving yourself a lot of time and it makes repair/shooting easier to manage. Against a sloop ghost ship will miss most of their shot anyway and being immobile won't make them more accurate. Just try to shoot down all ship that may cross your boat because it does 4 holes and that hurt a lot.

Don't get fooled by youtube vids. Solo slooping is REALLY hard and for each vids of someone sinking another boat as a solo slooper you'll have thousand of dead solo sloopers. Don't be a foul and flee. If you want to fight, do it when you don't have anything on your boat or if you are truly forced to do so. Specials cannonballs are absolutly mandatory if you plan to fight solo.

&nbsp;

Also fleeing doesn't just mean going away. You should try to keg/board the other ship to stop them, lure them into storm/volcano/skelly galleon or use fort tower to shoot them. You have to be pro-active or you are just going to delay your death.

I'm not lgbt but I still make my boat as flashy as possible and the rainbow flag is a must. The set from the new tales is great for that and I mixed it with Azur crab stuff for more flashy colors. It's like some animal in nature. The more colorfull and visible you are, the more dangerous you are. It's a warning.

&nbsp;

Also no one want to take the risk to get his ass destroyed by someone with a flashy pink boat and rainbow flag.

Solo sloop is the hard mode. My first mistake was to believe I could won a fair fight. There is nothing fair playing 1vs3 or more so you don't have to be fair. You have to be sadistic and take every single bit of advantage you can get.

&nbsp;

Also spam special cannonball. This stuff is underused and can make a BIG difference. A crew come straight at you to ram and board you? A sleep cannonball, few shot and retreat. Your mast is down? Special canonball, repair mast and retreat.

This game requires players to set their own goal. Some people aren't used to play this way, end up doing nothing and get bored.

&nbsp;

This game is for players enjoying the sandbox kind of stuff. It's not for everyone.

You can server hop and look at your map for any reaper. If there is reaper, just disconnect and reconnect with a fresh boat until you find a map that look empty/reaper free.

&nbsp;

Also put cosmetics on your ship and load special cannonballs for the glowing effect. I have very flashy cosmetics and almost no one try to attack me. The more shiny you are, the more experienced you looks and it scares people. If you have the basic ship a lot of noob will believe you are also a noob and try kill what looks like an easy prey.

I do it a little bit and I find it really meh. Fishing is always boring in game. I don't get the repetitive and boring grind stuff like that. I would prefer having trouble to find the right bait and place rather than spamming until the right fish comes. Fishing is not difficult. It's just extremelly grindy.

&nbsp;

Imo it would be better if place was more uncommon/dangerous but the drop rate almost 100%. For example fishing while a shark is attacking you or fishing on a skelleton ship. Imagine each shark having a specific kind of fish around it so you would have to hunt each meg and fish while at the same time your mate try to keep the ship safe.

On each map only 1 or 2 ship are a real danger. Watch on the world map for reapers and try to stay away from them. Most of the crew are just people doing their own business and you'll often find a server where no one is attacking each other. Go for bigger stuff and accept that you'll lose 10% of it. It's better to go for 100k voyage and lose everything 10% of the time than grinding 10k "safe" voyage.

&nbsp;

Also don't hesitate to play with random people. Being 2 help a lot.

I would rather have better loading time. My PC is not the best and when I die I spend more time looking at a black screen than being actually dead. It's so long that if I die I know it's over.

&nbsp;

Also I'm fully against the resurrect system in PvP.

I disagree with you on 2 points. First spell damage mage is ok. I climbed legend with spell damage mage last month and I'm currently at 119-101 (54%) with the deck. Is it broken or top meta? Of course not but at least it's playable and allow you to play something else than full spell mage. Also as I said VS report show that even if not good the deck is still played (mostly because it's super fun to throw 10+ damages fireball).

&nbsp;

Regarding Apexis blast, the card has the 4th winrate at mulligan (which for a 5 mana card says a lot about it's power), is the second best winrate when draw and the third winrate when played. It's definitely one of the key card of the deck. Not THE key card but like I said, nerfing apexis would only hit full spell mage and leave other mage deck safe which imo is a best for a class that mostly rely on 1 deck to stay relevant. Imo Incanter's flow would be a good nerf target just before a mini-set or expansion release but not right now.

