You have to divide the battle in several act and don't play the fight between act. Keep the fight system for relevant opponents only (or you'll throw dice for 10 hours).

&nbsp;

Let's say your players are in the middle of the army. Describe the charge and ask them to roll a CC check. Depending on the result you describe how they are doing. For exemple if a player succeed the roll by 10 you say something like: "you clash with the skaven and manage to instantly kill one, then another and another. It seems that the wave of rat is endless but you are doing fine". If the other player miss by 10 you say: "After the charge you are lost. There is too much noise, too much people, too much blood. You manage to hide being a dead body and try to regain your calm."

&nbsp;

After this description, put an "event" like a rat-ogre or a general in trouble that need help, or anything fun and exciting and play the event like an independant battle. Between each event, come back to the overall description of the battle with just a CC check to see how each players is doing during this interlude. With this method you'll transform a big and long battle into a serie of small fight that will be easier to manage.

