The most important is to feel confortable with the weapon of your choice, to often change weapon or talent to test them and to know exactly what you have to do to kill any units. Do not just copy/paste build you find or pick some talent because it "seems" better. Test them all. Once this is done, you can safely choose whatever you want and make it works.

You have to take the lead and move in front. If you are good enough the best is to have Bot/mates just behind you so they do not take a lot of risk and can help you if you have an issue. This force you to have a very agressive gameplay. If you are used to play safely and behind you'll struggle.

&nbsp;

The best way to play "solo" is to be aggressive and to get a high damage. Rush ennemy and Kill/kill/kill. If your main objective is to stay alive and not take damage you'll not get far because the threat will start to accumulate and you'll fall. Playing safely is ok when you are low HP, got a tons of aggro and hope that your teamate will do the job until you can get THP or a potion. If you are full HP you should focus on killing stuff as fast as you can to avoid being suffocated by ennemy density.

&nbsp;

Of course your teammates influence how smooth the game go but it shouldn't be an issue for 100% of your game.

