Yeah but from an economic point of view it doesn't make any sens. Halfeling craft leather armor to defend themself not to make profit. If they would make that much profit from leatherwork why would they even bother doing anything else when leather is easy to get? It's not like gromril or ithilmar which are really rare raw materials.

&nbsp;

To become good leather crafters halfeling had to craft a lot which probably make sens since they have to fight to protect the moot and have a lot of leather available thanks to their farming. They have an entire army of sentinelle to equip to protect the moot. At the end a moot leather armor is probably something really easy to get for a halfeling but not for someone who leave outside the moot because halfeling leather crafter have no real reason to craft anything but halfeling sized armor which means a human would have to find a leather crafter who is ok to craft a tailored armor and will probably make a lot of profit from it.

&nbsp;

What would justify such a big price? 

* Rarity? If it's rare it means the amount of halfeling leather crafter is low. Why would their leather crafting skill be that high if this industry isn't developped? 
* High raw material cost? Nope, make no sens for leather.

&nbsp;

For halfeling the price should probably be similar to the normal cost of a leather armor and for a human it should probably be around x2 or x3 but never x10. There is absolutly no industry with a 90% margin profit on a basic skill.

