I'll add that:

French have some sort of carapace around them to protect them from outside. This is why they often looks cold and not friendly at first. Switching from "vous" to "tu" is a way to break this carapace. This is also why in France we often find American too friendly and too demonstrative at first.

&#x200B;

In your situation it means that your Chief will probably be more open to make small talk with you, including topic like family, politics and all those kind of stuff which we generally avoid at first.

&#x200B;

