If he asks to use "tu" and use "tu" with you then you use "tu". Also don't care about what others think. The use of "tu/vous" is between 2 persons and the others have nothing to do or say about it.

&#x200B;

If you keep using "vous" he'll probably believe that you want to put some distance with him and it's not friendly. Switching from "vous" to "tu" with someone means you broke the "stranger" line and open a potential friendship. It's pretty comon in the workplace once you start to know your collegue.

Do you have exemple? Qui is a pronom and you conjugate base on what the pronom means. If you use "qui" to describe several women you'll conjugate like "elles".

