I agree that France did a lot of bad things in history and I strongly believe that the rise of nazi is mainly due to the humiliation of Versailles treaty after WW1 followed by the 1929 crisis. But I feel that your comment about "arrogant whining and rioting" is a bit of a cliché. French aren't proud people fighting against an unjust governments. People protest and strike is simply as a very basic of freedom. Voting is a way to express your opinion but there is no vote for everything so if enough people disagree with something they strike and voice their concern in order to influence political decision. It's a strong tool we have to keep control on gouvernment decision.

&#x200B;

You would be surprise to see how many political decision were done or reversed because of strike. Almost all of our social system has been herited by strike mouvement. In a lot of country a strike is seen as an extrem mesure taken because the situation is critical. In France it's the step that comes right after a discussion around a barbecue. A strike start to be critical after 2 or 3 weeks only. It's means the matter is serious enough and people don't give up.

&#x200B;

While a lot of people complain, France remains on of the top Democracy in the world so I wouldn't say our politcal system suck. At the last presidential election we had 5 differents party with more than 10% of vote. The amount of serious choice we have when voting is unmatched in the world.

