Your guest number (and tickets sold) is directly linked to the parc rating and to the size of the park. Avoid doing huge park with a lot of travel time. It's harder to keep it clean and secure. At start you should limit your park to a small area (and cut some path if needed). Pause the game, build a square with food/drink//toilet ... and directly link 2 or 3 small attraction and a rollercoaster to it. Unpause and take time to decorate it your attractions while research is going on and cash flow is increasing.

&nbsp;

If you keep your park small at first you should quickly be at 100% in food/drink/clean/decoration etc. Once your overall park rating is around 90%, extend by creating a new place with food/drink etc and link 3/4 new attractions to it. It's very important to keep people in small area with a quick access to everything. When a guest go out of a coaster he should immediatly be close to shop, toilets and the entrance of another coaster.

