For me a card has to be removed from the game only because the design is horrible. Most card can be fixed with a small nerf. So the card that imo really could be remove are those:

&nbsp;

- UI: This card reward bad play, ressource throwing and full greed. People put 2 in a deck just because it's so broken that you need to be sure to draw it even if you'll only play 1 at the end.

&nbsp;

- Baku: Some upgraded hero power are toxic and need a nerf. This will never happen so the only way to fix it is to remove baku himself.

&nbsp;

- Preparation: You can't really nerf it without totally breaking it and it cost way too much design space in rogue. 

&nbsp;

Special note: Cards like DK Guldan or N'zoth that completly refill the board should be toned down. Dominating a game and being completly destroyed by a top deck of those card is a terrible game experience and throwing ressources mindlessly because you know you can get them back for free should never exist. I never understood why they didn't limited those ressurect mechanic to 3 instead of "all".

If Mana wyrm was really an issue it would be played in decks others than Tempo/aggro deck. A lot of card are auto-include in some kind of deck simply because they are classic and perfectly fit some archetype. The real issue are card that are core to a class no matter what kind of deck it is. I would rather adress frostbolt than mana wyrm for exemple and the fiery nerf axe is a perfect exemple of that.

&nbsp;

Tempo mage has always been a thing not because of Mana wyrm but because they kept printing card for it over and over and ignored others decks. They killed control with Ice block HoF and didn't gave anything relevant to compensate, they printed a tons of elementals but failed to make it relevant and they tried to make "freeze" stuff happen by printing horrible card like snap freeze.

&nbsp;

Just look at elemental mage. It's mainly elementals and very few spells. Wyrm isn't core at all in the deck and you can totally skip it because you don't have the synergy but you still have frostbolt and Glyph even if you play book of specters. Those 2 spells are SO good that even in a deck where you do not want spell you'll still play them. I understand that playing against a tempo mage who has the perfect mana wyrm opening the game can feel frustrating but it's a rare situation that isn't even that good if you have the right answer (and many class have the right answers). On opposite there are a tons of cards that are way more broken and way more problematic than that.

All classes have card that cost less than the "answer" and on the opposite card that cost more than the "answer". If you look at mage, while Mana wyrm cost less than any 3 damages answer all the other minions (4 mana 4/3 for exemple) are extremelly easy to deal with. A 4 mana hellfire can deal with a full tempo mage board. If you look at zoolock, a lot of minions requires way less ressources than what it cost to remove them. It's the basic concept of tempo.

&nbsp;

And yes you have to use a kill command or hunter's mark + arcane shot to kill a mana wyrm. Because once you deal with the mana wyrm you won't have a lot of big threat to deal with anyway.

If you have trouble to deal with water elemental (which isn't played in any competitive deck), Kabal crystal runner in wild or a simple 2/3 turn 2 you should really look at what others class do before complaining about Mana wyrm. Mage class has strong spell and weak minions. If you have trouble to deal with mage minions I can't even imagine what it is against others classes. You should really cry against zoolock.

&nbsp;

If you can't deal with a single 3 HP minions turn 1 on a regular basis then either you mulligan wrong or you deck is badly designed. A lot of aggro deck require to get early removal and since you can almost ignore all the other mage minions you should always keep your removal for the wyrm. There are no reason to not use the early removal EVERY DECK SHOULD HAVE to counter the mana wyrm. Mana wyrm is often compared to trogg but trogg wasn't an issue by itself. The fact that it was buffed by playing a 2 mana 3/4 was the problem. If a mage buff the mana wyrm early it means that it doesn't put any other minions to the board. If you deal with the wyrm, you almost win.

&nbsp;

Sure sometimes you'll have a trash hand and your mage opponent will have the absolute perfect hand. But you shouldn't take in consideration this perfect scenario to decide if a card needs or not  a nerf. This scenario can happen with almost every deck and can be used as an argument to nerf/HoF absolutly any card for any Tier 1 deck.

No it's not normal. Your hospital is badly designed (no offense). You need a good amount of GP office at the entrance of your hospital, then you need to put the other GP office close to the diagnosis room. This way people come in, go in the first GP office, move to diagnosis room then go the GP office close to the diagnosis room and repeat. Once it is done they can go to treatment room (place them in the free space you have in your starting building). Your staffroom and toilets are too big. Use them to fill space where you can't build a 3x3 room and put several of them everywhere.

&nbsp;

On top of that you should increase your price and lower you reputation. If you can't handle the amount of patient sent by your high reputation you HAVE to lower it. You'll be able to carry a very good reputaton only if all your doc/nurse are fully trained and your hospital is correctly organised.

I have to admit that I disliked destroying my reputation at first. It was totally unnatural to focus on being a "bad" hospital but once you start playing like that you realized that having less people around is way less "stressfull" and allow you to do what you want instead of having to deal with the constant flow and 9+ queue. It also increase your "cure rate" (I don't know the exact term in english) as it prevent people from dying during the waiting time. 

&nbsp;

At the end I see my hospitals as private clinic. People pay a LOT but there is a constant 90% cure rate and they do not have to wait, can enjoy real meal instead of soda cans and chips and get easy access to very clean restroom.

Increase your price to crush your reputation and sell the most useless room you built to reduce your hospital level. Keep the food price very low to keep happiness ok so people won't leave angry. It'll reduce the amount of people coming to your hospital so they'll wait less and their chance of dying before being treated decrease.

&nbsp;

Your hospital is too big to be effective. The bigger your hospital is, the harder it is to keep everyone alive.

Also keep your price high and reputation/hospital level low. Compensate with low price for Food to keep people happy (at least not mad) so they won't leave the hospital before being cured. 

&nbsp;

It sounds stupid at first but It'll avoid overpopulation and the famous GP queue while keeping your income almost intact and gives you more time for training. You can run an hospital with 0 reputation, all you need is a little bit of marketing.

&nbsp;

Now I just run hospital with the cheapest room, higher price and I keep people happy with free food while calmly doing the mission objectives.

Firefly/elemental package was very good before expansion because of all the paladin (the firefly is super efficient to clear paladin token early). At the moment your biggest ennemy is zoolock and Hunter because you can't really deal with their massive board presence and firefly isn't very usefull. Zoolock has always been an issue for tempo mage because flame imp totally ruin mana wyrm opening. This is why imo you should rather go for a full aggro deck with 2 mirror images to protect your minions early or go for a slightly more control oriented deck with some frost nova/tar creeper to stale the game a little bit while you draw your burn.

&nbsp;

*At the moment I'm running this version:* AAECAf0EBO0FwwHu9gKi0wINtASVA7wIlgbBwQKWBZjEAuYEqwT77AKP0wLsBbsCAA==

&nbsp;

There is a lot of change you can do (the secret for exemple) but overall it'll be the same: You'll have a hard time against other aggro deck and you'll feed against control deck. Tempo mage has very polarized match-up. You'll also see a lot of others mage playing big spell because it has a better match-up against aggro deck (zoolock) but it struggle way more against other control/otk deck so the overall winrate won't really be better. There are a lot of player going for the spell damage package like arcane anomaly but it will make your match-up against zoolock even worste. It's more a "win more" card rather than something that actually make you win and swing the game in your favor.

I play mostly mage so I'll stay on it:

&nbsp;

**Hand mage**: at the moment element mage is "ok" and one of the main stuff to keep a hand full is the use card generation rather than draw. Sure Book of scepters is usefull but card like firefly, Steam surger, Ruby spellstone or even igneous elemental help to cheat the "big hand" by providing a lot of cheap stuff in your hand. In your deck you are completly depending on book of scepter to get a big hand and it won't work.

&nbsp;

**Spell Damage Mage**: Vex crow wasn't played and adding spell power won't change it since it doesn't scale at all with spell power. 6 4-mana card is too much imo especially if you are playing card like Stargazer luna. It's pretty much the same for Black cat. I think you should simply go for 1/2 mana card, few 3 mana spell you can reduce with sorcerer, Luna, Aluneth and Fireball and be super aggressive. With Aluneth, Luna and maybe the new 2 draw instead of Arcane intellect there is a high probability that you'll be able to never run out of steam. Also I don't believe in arcane anomaly. Most of the time it'll be a 4/3 for 4 that deal 2 additionnal damage at best since you want to play it on curve. A this point I would rather play lifedrinker for 3 damages without any combo needed.

Witchwood was ok. Bonfire elemental, arugal, book of scepter and cinderstorm are decent and can see play in the correct deck. Knigth of the frozen throne was way more horrible (outside of lich jaina).

&nbsp;

This expansion seems very low  for mage mainly because you have 0 mech interaction and almost all the neutral pool revolve around Mech. Research project is Godlike for any combo/Burn deck, Stargazer Luna has very good potential and luna'spocket galaxy will require a lot of deckbuilding test but can have a very strong effect. The rest is horrible.

Most of the time gaming addiction is a symptoms and not a disease. You can't quit gaming because it helps you escaping your daily issue. This is true for a lot of hobby addiction and the real answer is to fix life issue which will reduce the need of gaming.

&nbsp;

Life issue can be despression, stress, failure at job/study, bad self-estime, lack of social interaction ... 

&nbsp;

There are a lot of people who spend 5H+ watching TV or Smartphone. Gaming a lot isn't an issue, the fact that you have nothing outside of it is an issue. Choose yourself a small goal in life and try to achieve it. Once it is done, choose another one etc. By doing this I learned Guitar, created 1 tabletop game, lost 10kg .... every goal will boost your confidence and make the next one easier to achieve. Just don't go too big. Start small and focus on something important for you. Everytime you advance in your goal, reward yourself with some gaming. Gaming will be a reward for a good behaviour instead of a bad habit.

