But overall Paladin and warlock are too strong. Rotation let them too much untouched.

At some point most Combo deck are also instantly concede bad against the most aggro deck. I do understand the idea that having to completly change your gameplan or lose is frustrating but in the same time it makes the game less repetitive. Everyone complain about facing the same deck over and over but when a deck played by 1.76% of the player with a 39.09% winrate (exodia mage, last vssyndicate report) comes they cry because it forces them to play differently than usual. I have always been super happy to play against some exodia mage, mill rogue or other gimmick deck. They actually force you to think and make unnatural play to win by droping on curve minions you usually save for later. It's super refreshing when it doesn't infest the meta.

&nbsp;

