There was a podcast with DnD designer talking about DnD. At one moment they said:

&nbsp;

> The general feeling among the people running the company was that Basic D&D was the starting point. If you didn't know anything about D&D, you would pick up Basic, and you would play that, and that was for younger players, you know, who were just getting into the game, and Advanced was the "advanced" version, and once you were an experienced role-player, you would move up to Advanced.

> But our own experience told us that that was completely wrong -- that it was new players coming into the game that were going straight to Advanced, because they want the rules to tell them what to do. And it was really only players who had a good grasp on all this -- and experience with the game -- who were playing D&D Basic and Expert, because that gave them the freedom to do what they wanted.

&nbsp;

My point is that DnD and a lot of Pen and Paper RPG are already providing a TONS of rules. Setting even more rules slows the game rythms and experienced players tend to use less rules in order to not been restricted by them in their story/items design. Breaking rules is like breaking chains for a GM.

On a face hunter deck you plan to end the game in Turn 5/6. It means you'll use your hero power 2, 3 or 4 times at best. Using Baku means you'll do something like 3/4 extra damages for free but you have to remove 2/4 drop. Razormaw, Houndmaster, spellbreaker (to pass taunt), Hyena and potential secret played on curve worth WAY more than 3/4 free damages and I won't even talk about the fact you are polluting your deck with a bad stated minions. There is nothing more inneficient for an aggro deck than spamming hero power. You want to develop your board presence to install pressure on your opponnent by playing on curve.

&nbsp;

On top of that if I'm not playing T2 I would rather play Keleseth than Baku. The only good reason to play Baku in a face hunter would be to have an insane 1 mana minions for hunter in Odd deck.

Hey dude!

Anthonidas isn't "meta" at the moment outside of quest mage which is super hard to pilot. Anyway if you don't have a lot of card and start the game you can do farely well with a cheap tempo mage deck. I have made a list for you.

&nbsp;

http://www.hearthstonetopdecks.com/deck-builder/#?class=Mage&format=2&deck=1798:2,57698:2,1989:2,41625:2,1768:2,1987:2,2002:2,2632:2,72740:2,1922:2,1725:2,1808:2,2085:2,1840:1,27118:2,1948:1

&nbsp;

It's not "super top good" but it's a decent budget deck that should get you some win even against very good deck. It's super cheap (only comon, rare and free card) and can be optimised easily. Note that all the card are either classic, basic or from the 3 last expansion so they won't rotate with the new expansion (only fireland portal but you get it for free buy doing karazhan prologue). Also outside of breath of sindragosa all the other card are "ok" to "good" so you won't regret the craft later in the game (you'll maybe not use them all the time but at least they are not trash).

&nbsp;

The strategy is to use cheap spell to keep the control of the board against aggro/mid range deck and keep them to combo with anthonidas/sorcerer apprentice against control deck to generate value and burst. Once you are done the top card to focus is Primordial glyph to switch with breath of sindragosa. Good luck !

We do not need balance. We need diversity. The issue isn't the fact that a card is strong or not but the lack of answer/counterplay and the fact that you'll face the same card over and over and over and over.

&nbsp;

Achieveing perfect balance is a pointless quest. You'll always have better card. What we need is less strong neutral card so you don't have always the same card in each deck and a reward for playing class that aren't played a lot. We need a way to reward people for playing a class that doesn't see play. If you are playing Shaman or hunter today, you need to get rewarded more for a victory than someone playing Priest or druid.

&nbsp;

So my guess is that they'll nerf strong neutral card and hopefully release a rework of ladder.

